cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Se usi Kite, citalo come indicato qui. / If you use Kite, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Kite: hybrid gaze keyboard for augmentative and alternative communication"
abstract: >-
  Kite is an open on-screen gaze keyboard for augmentative and alternative
  communication, for Linux, with the Tobii Eye Tracker 4C. A key fires when
  the gaze settles after the saccade that brings it there, after a time that
  depends on how likely the letter is; likely keys invisibly grow their hit
  areas through Bayesian decoding; the pupil, compensated for screen
  luminance, estimates cognitive load and can lengthen the timing. It includes
  an Italian corrector, local neural speech output and learned phrases. Gaze
  data come from the tobii4c-linux driver.
authors:
  - family-names: Blescia
    given-names: Antonio
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/ablescia/Kite"
url: "https://smartchair.it/ricerche/kite/"
keywords:
  - eye tracking
  - gaze typing
  - dwell time
  - augmentative and alternative communication
  - assistive technology
  - pupillometry
  - Tobii Eye Tracker 4C
# La versione non è indicata: Zenodo la prende dal tag della release.
